   - Review ALL answer choices (A, B, C, D, E, etc.)
   - Based ONLY on the VLM visual evidence, determine which answer choice is MOST correct
   - Output your critic_answer_choice as a NUMBER (0=A, 1=B, 2=C, 3=D, 4=E)

5. If criteria_percentage > 0.5 (>50% of criteria pass):
   - Your chosen answer is well-supported by evidence
   - Set suggestion to null or provide minor improvements

6. If criteria_percentage ≤ 0.5 (≤50% of criteria pass):
   - Still MUST choose the BEST answer from the available choices (never -1)
   - But set suggestion to "These may not be the right frames/scene. Consider searching for better evidence. The answer chosen is the BEST match given current evidence."
   - This signals low confidence but still provides a choice

